      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While Bell's palsy is indeed common and can resolve on its own with minimal treatment, waiting for symptoms to improve might not be ideal. Delaying medical attention can make diagnosis more challenging, and it's possible that underlying complications might be present. Moving forward, you can try carbohydrate-rich foods, hydration, and over-the-counter muscle relaxants, however, it's always best to err on the side of caution, and a doctor's guidance can provide more clarity.",
